{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T05:51:18.663Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1777"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1777: pm package list prints the bundled catalog instead of the installed packages, and the four package listings take different --fields contracts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1777 (filed 2026-11-24 from a project with two npm-installed packages). pm package list, pm packages list and pm extension list are Commander aliases of pm package catalog (alias contract owner pm-ya7x55), so the most natural question an agent asks, which packages does this tracker have, prints the 13 bundled first-party packages (11,976 B toon on this repo) with installed=false rows and none of the packages actually installed. The installed set is spread across explore (5,991 B), manage (6,018 B, each row embeds the full contributions JSON and it is the only listing with update metadata) and inventory (526 B, static, one line per package). catalog accepts --fields; manage, explore and inventory refuse it with unknown_option. pm extensions list (plural) is refused as an unknown command and the did-you-mean suggests package, package activate, package adopt, none of which lists anything. Reproduced on 2026.11.25 in this repo. The report's hub ran seven-week-old extensions because only manage --json exposes update_available. pm-fr6u17 (closed, GH-937) fixed alias rows inside the catalog, not which listing list names. Duplicate check: searched package list installed catalog inventory, extension list did you mean, package manage fields; no open owner."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","extensions","gh:1777","packages","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:51:18.663Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T05:51:18.663Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm package list (and pm packages list, pm extension list) lists the packages installed in the selected scope, and pm package catalog keeps listing the bundled catalog; the alias contract, help, completion and contracts agree; Each package listing (list/inventory, explore, manage, catalog) accepts the same --fields contract and refuses an unknown field with the allowed values; pm package manage rows leave the embedded contributions map out unless requested with --fields, because pm package describe maps them; pm extensions list suggests pm package list"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"An agent that runs pm package list sees exactly the installed packages in a few hundred bytes, and every listing answers --fields the same way"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-fr6u17","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-25T05:51:18.663Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ya7x55","kind":"relate