{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T08:10:09.508Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-25T08:10:09.507Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 1 fixes on the listing side: pm package --global list (scope switch before the verb) now stays on the static no-activation path (Codex P1); explore/manage validate --fields at action admission, before adoption, remote checks or observation writes (Codex P2); pm extension explore/manage --fields keep their subcommand route instead of the legacy root rewrite (Codex P2); catalog --fields uses the shared parser, so its refusal carries the whole catalog domain as allowed_values / legal_domain, keeping its curated example (Codex P2, Greptile); the shared fields tool metadata names package row keys and adds a package example (Codex P3); the inflected did-you-mean follows operands with the bootstrap scanner, so pm extensions --json list and --author <value> forms resolve to package list (Codex P3); pm extension list --help now shows the inventory help bundle (CodeRabbit; the cause was a missing extension inventory help entry, not the positional action table)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T08:10:09.508Z"}],"before_hash":"8ffed9223b8753adaf410c511d16b17d399630c0e3404252ab3af52b69c72caa","after_hash":"c4bb09b1a755d250a417ea31365a8610f3981745479c2f42fc8cf5fb705d667a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"85fe0caf5662d7761f89292291215743f7bbd6631372b55721df73483f14e7eb"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.772Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.771Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2 listing fixes: the static detector skips root switches and valued root options before the verb (pm package --offline list, --ref v1 list) without reading a value as the verb; bootstrap resolves the package leaf past a scope switch so repeated --fields accumulate (pm package --project list --fields a --fields b); flat MCP/SDK fields now hoist on the root package action, so package-explore/manage/catalog honor a flat fields parameter; pm package list refuses row-shaping read-output controls with read_output_surface_unsupported instead of silently ignoring them (--output-format and --output-budget unbounded still apply); listing --fields refusals carry code invalid_argument_value and recovery.allowed_values with the whole domain for SDK and MCP callers."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T08:47:44.772Z"}],"before_hash":"c4bb09b1a755d250a417ea31365a8610f3981745479c2f42fc8cf5fb705d667a","after_hash":"fd4eb32b289fa51f1f7480beab1c68067abb0f6bdad1d0845faef64bfcdc9fef","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4544fc965cef2d0174b4babc161530cfd5956c06baec2ad6c17957d874adc1ae"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.997Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.996Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 listing fixes: one shared lifecycle verb parser (resolveLifecycleVerb in the SDK bootstrap) now serves static selection, bootstrap leaf resolution and plural-noun recovery, so pm --no-changed-fields package list and pm package --offline list stay static (noun found with the host-option grammar), pm package --offline list x --fields=a --fields=b accumulates, and pm extensions --ref v1 list suggests package list. SDK/MCP dispatch of the static listing is recorded as scope on the follow-up listing item."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-25T09:57:02.997Z"}],"before_hash":"fd4eb32b289fa51f1f7480beab1c68067abb0f6bdad1d0845faef64bfcdc9fef","after_hash":"e92ad69a7d94df9a39e3c1b512fe5506e0fae48655919b0e0f1ba6a8b9eee6f2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4be2064bd56d33a4da663a7235af8466ccc12a021bc736fb1928a9440de87e7b"}
